@startuml UnifiedLogBERT Full Pipeline with Train Result Block

' === Стили ===
skinparam defaultFontSize 10
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor Black
  BackgroundColor LightCyan
}

' ========================
' 0. AZURE DEVOPS API (SOURCE)
' ========================
rectangle "Azure DevOps API\n(REST endpoint)" as azure_api

' ========================
' 1. GET LOGS SCRIPT
' ========================
rectangle "get_logs Script\n(REST API Call)" as get_logs

note right of get_logs
  Operations:\n
  • Input: pipeline_id, build_id\n
  • REST API: GET /_apis/build/builds/{buildId}/logs\n
  • Output: raw log content (as-is)\n
  • Handles: pagination, authentication, retries\n
  • Output: raw_logs (with timestamps, ##[section], etc.)
end note

azure_api --> get_logs : raw log content

' ========================
' 2. RAW LOGS (ORIGINAL OUTPUT FROM AZURE DEVOPS)
' ========================
rectangle "Raw Log Output\n(Original, unprocessed)\n2020-11-12T06:14:33.7066124Z ##[section]Starting: Prepare job Job_1\n2020-11-12T06:14:33.7222246Z ContinueOnError: False\n2020-11-12T06:14:33.7222246Z TimeoutInMinutes: 180\n2020-11-12T06:14:33.7222246Z CancelTimeoutInMinutes: 5\n2020-11-12T06:14:33.7222246Z Expand:\n2020-11-12T06:14:33.7222246Z   ########## System Pipeline Decorator(s) ##########\n\n2020-11-12T06:14:33.7222246Z   Begin evaluating template 'system-pre-steps.yml'\nEvaluating: eq('true', variables['system.debugContext'])\nExpanded: eq('true', Null)\nResult: False\nEvaluating: resources['repositories']['self']\nExpanded: Null\nResult: False\nFinished evaluating template 'system-pre-steps.yml'\n********************************************************************************\nTemplate and static variable resolution complete. Final runtime YAML document:\nsteps: []\n\n2020-11-12T06:14:33.7378501Z   MaxConcurrency: 0\n2020-11-12T06:14:33.7378501Z ##[section]Finishing: Prepare job Job_1" as raw_logs

get_logs --> raw_logs

' ========================
' 3. CLEAN STEP: REMOVE NOISE
' ========================
rectangle "Clean Step\n(Remove Noise)" as clean_step

note right of clean_step
  Operations:\n
  • Remove timestamps: \"2020-11-12T...Z\"\n
  • Remove \"##[section]Finishing: ...\"\n
  • Remove separators: \"********************************************************************************\"\n
  • Remove empty lines and extra indentation\n
  • Preserve only: content lines + \"##[section]Starting: ...\"\n
  → Output: clean, line-by-line, no metadata
end note

raw_logs --> clean_step

' ========================
' 4. PREPARE STEP: STRUCTURE & TAGGING
' ========================
rectangle "Prepare Step\n(Structure & Tagging)" as prepare_step

note right of prepare_step
  Operations:\n
  • Extract section/task headers: \"##[section]Starting: Prepare job Job_1\" → \"<TFS_Section> Prepare job Job_1\"\n
  • Normalize dynamic values: \"TimeoutInMinutes: 180\" → \"TimeoutInMinutes: <*>\"\n
  • Normalize task names: \"Task         : Set build version\" → \"<TFS_Task> Set build version\"\n
  • Remove redundant prefixes: \"  \" → no leading spaces\n
  • Output: structured, tag-based log stream\n
  → No noise, no timestamps, no metadata — only semantic structure
end note

clean_step --> prepare_step

' ========================
' 5. CLEANED LOGS (INPUT TO DRAIN3)
' ========================
rectangle "Cleaned Log Input\n(pre-processed)\n<TFS_Section> Prepare job Job_1\nContinueOnError: False\nTimeoutInMinutes: <*>\nCancelTimeoutInMinutes: <*>\nExpand:\n<TFS_Decorator>\nBegin evaluating template 'system-pre-steps.yml'\nEvaluating: eq('true', variables['system.debugContext'])\nExpanded: eq('true', Null)\nResult: False\nEvaluating: resources['repositories']['self']\nExpanded: Null\nResult: False\nFinished evaluating template 'system-pre-steps.yml'\nTemplate and static variable resolution complete. Final runtime YAML document:\nsteps: []\nMaxConcurrency: 0" as cleaned_logs

prepare_step --> cleaned_logs

' ========================
' 6. DRAIN3 OUTPUT FILES
' ========================
package "Drain3 Output Files" {
  rectangle "drain_templates.json\n{ \"E1\": \"<TFS_Section> <*>\",\n  \"E2\": \"ContinueOnError: False\",\n  \"E3\": \"TimeoutInMinutes: <*>\",\n  \"E4\": \"Got build number: <*>\",\n  \"E5\": \"Task was started\",\n  \"E6\": \"Final runtime YAML document: steps: []\" }" as templates
  rectangle "drain_sequences.jsonl\n{ \"pipeline_id\": \"109952\", \"event_seq\": [\"E2\",\"E3\",\"E4\",\"E5\",\"E6\",...] }" as sequences
  rectangle "drain_mapping.jsonl\n{ \"event_id\": \"E2\", \"template\": \"ContinueOnError: False\", \"section_name\": \"Prepare job Job_1\" }" as mapping
  rectangle "drain_state.json\n(compressed tree state)\nSerialized Drain3 tree:\n- depth: 4\n- sim_threshold: 0.6\n- max_children: 200\n- node structure\n→ Used for incremental processing\n→ Restores clustering state" as state
}

cleaned_logs --> templates : parsed by Drain3
templates --> mapping : maps template → event_id
mapping --> sequences : builds event_seq per pipeline

' ========================
' 7. BUILD VOCAB
' ========================
rectangle "build_vocab Script" as build_vocab

note right of build_vocab
  Operations:\n
  • Input: drain_templates.json\n
  • Output: event_vocab.json\n
  • Special tokens:\n
    - [PAD] → 0\n
    - [UNK] → 1\n
  • Maps: \"E1\" → 2, \"E2\" → 3, ...\n
  • vocab_size = len(event_ids) + 2\n
  • Used for tokenizing event_seq
end note

templates --> build_vocab

' === Vocab as separate element ===
rectangle "event_vocab.json" as vocab

build_vocab --> vocab

note right of vocab
  { \"[PAD]\": 0,\n
    \"[UNK]\": 1,\n
    \"E1\": 2,\n
    \"E2\": 3,\n
    ... }\n
  → Used to convert event_id → index
end note

' ========================
' 8. PREPARE WINDOWS
' ========================
rectangle "prepare_windows Script" as prepare_windows

note right of prepare_windows
  Operations:\n
  • Input: drain_sequences.jsonl, event_vocab.json\n
  • Splits: 85% train, 10% val, 5% test\n
  • Creates sliding windows:\n
    - window = event_seq[i:i+L]\n
    - target = event_seq[i+L]\n
  • Outputs:\n
    - train.pt, val.pt, test.pt (PyTorch tensors)\n
    - train_meta.jsonl (metadata per window)\n
  • Format: torch.save(dataset, 'train.pt')
end note

sequences --> prepare_windows
vocab --> prepare_windows

' === PyTorch Dataset as separate element ===
rectangle "PyTorch Dataset\ntrain.pt / val.pt / test.pt\n(archive with data.pkl, data/0, ...)" as pytorch_dataset
rectangle "train_meta.jsonl\n{ \"pipeline_id\": \"137437\", \"build_id\": \"26599574\", \"section_name\": \"Download files from Git\", \"section_bucket\": 1481, \"target_pos_in_section\": 64, \"window_idx_in_section\": 0 }\n{ ... }" as meta

prepare_windows --> pytorch_dataset
prepare_windows --> meta

' ========================
' 9. MODEL INPUTS
' ========================
rectangle "Tokenized Event IDs\ninput_ids = [2,3,4]\n(B=256, L≤512)" as input_tokens
rectangle "Section Bucket ID\nsec_ids\n(B=256,)\nsection_buckets=2048" as input_bucket

pytorch_dataset --> input_tokens
meta --> input_bucket

' ========================
' 10. LOGBERT MODEL BLOCK (CORRECTED)
' ========================
package "LogBERT Model" {
  rectangle "Token Embedding\nvocab_size=V\nd_model=512" as token_emb
  rectangle "Section Embedding\nnum_emb=2048\ndim=512" as section_emb
  rectangle "Add Embeddings\n(B, L, 512)" as add_emb
  rectangle "Positional Embedding\nmax_len=512" as pos_emb
  rectangle "Transformer Encoder\n6 layers, 8 heads\nFF=2048, dropout=0.1" as transformer
  rectangle "LayerNorm (last token)\nh[:, -1, :] → (B, 512)" as norm
  rectangle "LM Head\nLinear(512 → V)" as lm_head
  rectangle "logits\n(B, V)" as output_logits

  ' === Internal Transformer Nodes (Optional, can be removed for clarity) ===
  rectangle "Self-Attention\n(Q,K,V)" as att
  rectangle "FFN\n512→2048→512" as ffn

  ' Training components inside LogBERT
  rectangle "Loss\nCrossEntropy" as loss
  rectangle "Optimizer\nAdamW" as optimizer
  rectangle "Training Config" as train_config
}

input_tokens --> token_emb : (B,L)
input_bucket --> section_emb : (B,)
token_emb --> add_emb : (B,L,512)
section_emb --> add_emb : (B,1,512) broadcast
add_emb --> pos_emb : (B,L,512)
pos_emb --> transformer : (B,L,512)

' === Main data flow ===
transformer --> norm : (B,L,512) → (B,512)
norm --> lm_head : (B,512)
lm_head --> output_logits : (B,V)

' === Internal transformer processes (dotted) ===
transformer -[#Blue,dotted]-> att
att -[#Blue,dotted]-> ffn

' === Training flow ===
output_logits --> loss : logits (B,V)
loss --> optimizer : loss.backward()
optimizer --> train_config : update weights

' === Arrows with Colors ===
azure_api -[#Blue]-> get_logs : REST API call
get_logs -[#Orange]-> raw_logs : raw log content
raw_logs -[#Orange]-> clean_step : noisy, timestamped, unstructured
clean_step -[#DarkGreen]-> prepare_step : stripped, line-based
prepare_step -[#DarkGreen]-> cleaned_logs : structured, tag-based

templates -[#Purple]-> build_vocab : list of event templates
build_vocab -[#Purple]-> vocab : event_vocab.json

sequences -[#Teal]-> prepare_windows : event sequences
vocab -[#Teal]-> prepare_windows : mapping
prepare_windows -[#Teal]-> pytorch_dataset : train.pt, val.pt, test.pt
prepare_windows -[#Teal]-> meta : train_meta.jsonl

pytorch_dataset -[#DarkGreen]-> input_tokens : input_ids
meta -[#DarkGreen]-> input_bucket : sec_ids

' ========================
' 11. TRAINING OUTPUT ARTIFACTS
' ========================
rectangle "model.pt" as model_pt
rectangle "optimizer.pt" as optimizer_pt
rectangle "scaler.pt" as scaler_pt

train_config --> model_pt : torch.save(model.state_dict())
train_config --> optimizer_pt : torch.save(optimizer.state_dict())
train_config --> scaler_pt : torch.save(scaler.state_dict()) ' for AMP

' ========================
' 12. QUANTIZATION STEP
' ========================
rectangle "Quantize to INT8\n(torch.quantization)" as quantize

model_pt --> quantize

rectangle "model_quant.pt" as model_quant_pt

quantize --> model_quant_pt

' ========================
' 13. TRAIN RESULT BLOCK
' ========================
package "Train Result" {
  rectangle "model_quant.pt" as model_quant_pt_block
  rectangle "event_vocab.json" as vocab_block
  rectangle "drain_state.json" as state_block
  rectangle "drain_templates.json" as templates_block
}

model_quant_pt --> model_quant_pt_block
vocab --> vocab_block
state --> state_block
templates --> templates_block

' === NOTES ===
note right of pytorch_dataset
  PyTorch dataset archive:\n
  train.pt:\n
    - data.pkl: metadata\n
    - data/0, data/1, ...: tensor shards\n
    - version, byteorder, etc.\n
  → Loaded via torch.load()
end note

note right of meta
  Metadata per window:\n
  • pipeline_id, build_id\n
  • section_name → section_bucket\n
  • target_pos_in_section: position of target token\n
  • window_idx_in_section: window index\n
  → Used to inject section context
end note

note right of train_config
  Training Parameters:\n
  • batch_size: 256\n
  • lr: 1e-4\n
  • weight_decay: 0.01\n
  • grad_clip: 1.0\n
  • amp: true\n
  • seed: 42
end note

note right of model_pt
  Trained model weights:\n
  • state_dict()\n
  • Contains embeddings, transformer, LM head
end note

note right of optimizer_pt
  Optimizer state:\n
  • AdamW momentum, variance\n
  • Enables resume training
end note

note right of scaler_pt
  AMP scaler state:\n
  • Loss scaling factor\n
  • Prevents underflow in FP16
end note

note right of quantize
  Quantization:\n
  • Converts FP32 → INT8\n
  • Reduces model size by ~4x\n
  • Speeds up inference\n
  • Uses torch.quantization\n
  → Output: model_quant.pt
end note

caption UnifiedLogBERT: Full end-to-end pipeline with Train Result block\nAzure DevOps → Raw Logs → Clean → Prepare → Drain3 → Vocab → Windows → LogBERT (with training) → Train Result (model + vocab + drain files)
footer Created: November 10, 2025 | Includes training output and quantization

@enduml